@appointments
title: Placing your people
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: sanchez_leader = 1 and appoint_timer <= 0
on-arrival: appoint_timer = 4

= Placing your people

The plotters are only as strong as the posts they hold. Your Secretary of Organisation brings a list of positions that could go to people loyal to you. Barons' plotting: **[+ plot_word +]**. Loyalists in key posts: [+ loyalist_posts_text +].

- @app_posts: Fill one of the party's top posts
- @app_exec: Force critics out of the Federal Executive and co-opt sanchistas
- @app_cooptbarons: Bring the barons into the Federal Executive
- @app_fed: Back loyalist candidates against the barons in the regional federations
- @app_group: Replace the parliamentary group's leadership
- @app_statutes: Rewrite the statutes: members, not the Federal Committee, choose and remove the leader
- @root: Not now

@app_exec
subtitle: Costs party funds; secures the Executive so the critics cannot dissolve it by resigning; angers the faction you push out
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.placeLoyalists(Q, 'executive'); !}

Ábalos, Lastra and your inner circle take the Executive's key portfolios, and critics are eased out with posts elsewhere. The old guard calls it a purge.

@app_posts
title: The party's top posts
subtitle: Each post you hold with a loyalist makes you harder to remove; each critic you sack has friends

= The party's top posts

Who holds each post is on the Party tab.

- @post_org: Secretary of Organisation
- @post_deputy: Deputy Secretary-General
- @post_spokes: Spokesperson in Congress
- @post_president: President of the party
- @post_fcpres: President of the Federal Committee
- @root: Back

@post_org
title: Secretary of Organisation

= Secretary of Organisation

Runs the party machine: the census, the lists, the federations.

- @post_org_0: César Luena
- @post_org_1: José Luis Ábalos
- @post_org_2: Óscar López
- @post_org_3: Antonio Pradas

@post_org_0
subtitle: Your loyal organiser; no change if he holds it
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.appointPost(Q, 'org', 0); !}

[? if appoint_ok = 1 : César Luena is the new Secretary of Organisation. ?][? if appoint_ok = 0 : The Federal Committee votes your nominee down. The barons count it as a win. ?]

@post_org_1
subtitle: A hard-nosed sanchista operator: more loyalists, angrier barons
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.appointPost(Q, 'org', 1); !}

[? if appoint_ok = 1 : José Luis Ábalos is the new Secretary of Organisation. ?][? if appoint_ok = 0 : The Federal Committee votes your nominee down. The barons count it as a win. ?]

@post_org_2
subtitle: A moderniser bridge to the critics: calms the plot a little
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.appointPost(Q, 'org', 2); !}

[? if appoint_ok = 1 : Óscar López is the new Secretary of Organisation. ?][? if appoint_ok = 0 : The Federal Committee votes your nominee down. The barons count it as a win. ?]

@post_org_3
subtitle: A Díaz man: buys peace with the barons, costs you control of the machine
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.appointPost(Q, 'org', 3); !}

[? if appoint_ok = 1 : Antonio Pradas is the new Secretary of Organisation. ?][? if appoint_ok = 0 : The Federal Committee votes your nominee down. The barons count it as a win. ?]

