@post_fcpres
title: President of the Federal Committee

= President of the Federal Committee

Chairs the Committee that can remove you; elected by it, so it may refuse.

- @post_fcpres_0: Verónica Pérez
- @post_fcpres_1: Susana Sumelzo

@post_fcpres_0
subtitle: Díaz's ally from Seville, the incumbent
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.appointPost(Q, 'fcpres', 0); !}

[? if appoint_ok = 1 : Verónica Pérez is the new President of the Federal Committee. ?][? if appoint_ok = 0 : The Federal Committee votes your nominee down. The barons count it as a win. ?]

@post_fcpres_1
subtitle: An Aragonese loyalist: the Committee must agree
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.appointPost(Q, 'fcpres', 1); !}

[? if appoint_ok = 1 : Susana Sumelzo is the new President of the Federal Committee. ?][? if appoint_ok = 0 : The Federal Committee votes your nominee down. The barons count it as a win. ?]

@app_cooptbarons
subtitle: Gives up seats in the Executive; the plot cools and the barons feel heard
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.shiftExecutive(Q, 'Sanchismo', 'Regional Barons', 3); Q.plot -= 10; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 8; Q.sanchismo -= 3; !}

Three seats in the Executive go to people named by the regional presidents. It buys calm. It also brings the critics closer to the number they would need to bring the Executive down.

@app_fed
subtitle: A gamble: success breaks the barons' hold, failure makes them stronger
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.placeLoyalists(Q, 'federations'); !}

[? if loyalist_ok = 1 : Your candidates win the federation primaries in several regions. The barons' network has holes in it now. ?][? if loyalist_ok = 0 : The barons' candidates win, and they know who tried to unseat them. ?]

@app_group
subtitle: A loyal parliamentary group; the institutionalists grumble
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.placeLoyalists(Q, 'group'); !}

A new spokesperson and a new whip. The deputies will vote as you tell them.

@app_statutes
view-if: primary_won = 1 or sanchismo >= 60
subtitle: Needs a members' mandate; makes the leader much harder to remove
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; window.SpainGame.placeLoyalists(Q, 'statutes'); !}

A federal congress approves new statutes: the members elect and remove the Secretary-General, and the Federal Committee can no longer topple the leader on its own.

@dark_arts
title: The dark arts
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: dark_timer <= 0 and (sanchez_leader = 1 or leadership_exception_open = 1 or backbench = 1)
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.dark_timer = 6; !}

= The dark arts

Someone in your circle knows people who know how things are done: census lists that can be padded, journalists who will print a dossier, friends in other parties' internal races. It costs money, and it leaves fingerprints.

- @da_rig: Pad the membership census before the next party vote
- @da_meddle_pp: Help the weakest candidate in the PP's internal fight
- @da_meddle_up: Encourage Podemos's internal dissidents
- @da_sabotage_pp: Leak a dossier on a PP rival
- @da_sabotage_diaz: Leak a dossier on Susana Díaz's allies
- @da_no: No: if it came out, it would finish you

@da_rig
subtitle: Costs 2 in [+ spend_name +]. A few points in the next leadership vote or Federal Committee; if exposed, a scandal that turns it against you
choose-if: spendable >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 2 in [+ spend_name +].
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.darkArts(Q, 'rig'); } !}

[? if dark_exposed = 0 : New members appear on the lists of friendly local branches. Nobody asks where they came from. ?][? if dark_exposed = 1 : El País publishes the story: hundreds of "ghost members" signed up in your friends' branches. The Ethics Committee opens an inquiry, and the barons have a new weapon. ?]

@da_meddle_pp
subtitle: Costs 1 in [+ spend_name +]. A more divided PP; if exposed, relations with the PP collapse
choose-if: spendable >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 in [+ spend_name +].
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.darkArts(Q, 'meddle', 'pp'); } !}

[? if dark_exposed = 0 : Quiet help finds its way to the PP's least electable candidate. ?][? if dark_exposed = 1 : The PP discovers who has been helping its internal rebels. Génova calls it "an attack on democracy". ?]

@da_meddle_up
subtitle: Costs 1 in [+ spend_name +]. Podemos splits a little more; if exposed, relations with Podemos collapse
choose-if: spendable >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 in [+ spend_name +].
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.darkArts(Q, 'meddle', 'up'); } !}

[? if dark_exposed = 0 : Podemos's critics find they have more friends in the press than they expected. ?][? if dark_exposed = 1 : Iglesias produces the messages: the PSOE has been stirring Podemos's internal war. ?]

@da_sabotage_pp
subtitle: Costs 1 in [+ spend_name +]. Hurts the PP; if exposed, the scandal is yours
choose-if: spendable >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 in [+ spend_name +].
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.darkArts(Q, 'sabotage', 'pp'); } !}

[? if dark_exposed = 0 : The dossier runs on the front page. The PP's week is spent explaining. ?][? if dark_exposed = 1 : The dossier's source is traced back to Ferraz. The story is no longer the PP; it is you. ?]

@da_sabotage_diaz
view-if: year <= 2018
subtitle: Costs 1 in [+ spend_name +]. Weakens the plot against you; if exposed, the barons strike
choose-if: spendable >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 in [+ spend_name +].
on-arrival: {! if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.darkArts(Q, 'sabotage', 'diaz'); } !}

[? if dark_exposed = 0 : Stories about the Andalusian federation's finances unsettle Díaz's allies. ?][? if dark_exposed = 1 : The leak is traced to your team. The regional barons say you have declared war on your own party. ?]

@da_no
on-arrival: dark_timer = 2

You leave the dark arts to others.

@territorial_line
title: The territorial model
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: sanchez_leader = 1 and terr_timer <= 0
on-arrival: terr_timer = 6

= The territorial model

The PSOE's line on Spain's territorial model is **[+ const_word +]**. Granada in 2013 committed the party to a federal reform; the barons of the south want no part of anything that sounds like a concession to the independence movement.

- @terr_central: Recentralise: one Spain, equal everywhere
- @terr_union: Firmly unionist, inside the current Constitution
- @terr_fed: A federal reform of the Constitution
- @terr_pluri: Spain as a nation of nations
- @root: Leave the line where it is

@terr_central
title: Recentralise
subtitle: Unionist voters approve; the PSC suffers, Podemos gains.
on-arrival: {! Q.const_line -= 2; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 4; Q.progressives_dissent += 5; Q.rel_erc -= 8; Q.rel_pnv -= 6; Q.rel_cs += 5; !}

The PSOE proposes to recover powers for the State. In Barcelona, the PSC hears about it on the radio.

@terr_union
title: Firmly unionist
subtitle: The barons approve; nationalist partners cool.
on-arrival: {! Q.const_line -= 1; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 3; Q.rel_erc -= 4; Q.rel_pnv -= 2; !}

The Constitution, all of it, and nothing but.

@terr_fed
title: A federal reform
subtitle: The Socialist Left and the PSC approve; the barons grumble.
on-arrival: {! Q.const_line += 1; Q.progressives_dissent -= 3; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 3; Q.rel_erc += 3; Q.rel_pnv += 3; !}

The Granada declaration, dusted off and turned into a draft.

@terr_pluri
title: A nation of nations
subtitle: Nationalist partners warm sharply; Vox and the PP have a new attack line.
on-arrival: {! Q.const_line += 2; Q.progressives_dissent -= 4; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 8; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 4; Q.rel_erc += 6; Q.rel_pnv += 6; Q.rel_bildu = (Q.rel_bildu || 40) + 5; !}

The PSOE accepts that Spain contains several nations. Page says it is the end of the party he knew.

@europe_line
title: The PSOE and Europe
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_party
view-if: sanchez_leader = 1 and eurol_timer <= 0
on-arrival: eurol_timer = 6

= The PSOE and Europe

The PSOE's European line is **[+ eu_word +]**. Spain is among the most pro-European countries in the Union, but Brussels was also the troika and the austerity of 2010-12.

- @eu_skeptic: Stand up to Brussels on austerity
- @eu_realist: Pro-European, with conditions
- @eu_pro: Spain at the heart of Europe
- @eu_fed: A federal Europe: eurobonds, a common budget, a common army
- @root: Leave the line where it is

@eu_skeptic
title: Stand up to Brussels
subtitle: Workers and Podemos voters listen; Brussels and liberal voters frown.
on-arrival: {! Q.eu_line -= 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', -6); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { workers: 0.4, unemployed: 0.4, professionals: -0.4 }); } Q.modernisers_dissent += 5; !}

No more cuts dictated from abroad, says Sánchez.

@eu_realist
title: Pro-European, with conditions
subtitle: A balanced line.
on-arrival: {! Q.eu_line -= 0.8; Q.modernisers_dissent += 1; Q.progressives_dissent -= 1; !}

Europe, yes; this Europe, not entirely.

@eu_pro
title: Spain at the heart of Europe
subtitle: Brussels warms; professionals approve.
on-arrival: {! Q.eu_line += 0.8; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', 4); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { professionals: 0.3 }); } Q.modernisers_dissent -= 2; !}

Spain will be where Europe is decided.

@eu_fed
title: A federal Europe
subtitle: Brussels is delighted; Vox calls you Brussels's servant.
on-arrival: {! Q.eu_line += 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.intl(Q, 'eu', 8); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', { professionals: 0.4, students: 0.3 }); } Q.modernisers_dissent -= 3; Q.trade_unionists_dissent += 2; !}

Eurobonds, a common budget, a European army: the PSOE signs up for all of it.
